-- title:
--   Generating Pic⁰ of the Igusa curve by chart point differences
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subset\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137), i.e. $L$ adjoined with the coefficientwise images of that field of $q$-series. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$. Let $c_1:C_1\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and $c_2:C_2\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ be proper, geometrically integral and smooth of relative dimension $1$, and let $i_1,i_2$ be closed immersions of $C_1,C_2$ into the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model $\mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, each compatible with the structure morphisms; assume the images of $i_1$ and $i_2$ on points cover the whole $k$-fibre, that the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1\times_X C_2$ is reduced, and that its cardinality is a number $n>0$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ (a weight-one modular form, an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion, with nonvanishing reduction $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,k$), and write $\mathrm{Ig}=\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w$, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ generated over $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\,k\,M$ by the inverse of that reduction. Let $\mathcal{M}_1$ be a `CurveModel` for $\mathrm{Ig}$ over $k$ (a proper integral curve, smooth of relative dimension $1$, with function field identified with $\mathrm{Ig}$ and closed points in bijection with the places of $\mathrm{Ig}/k$), together with an isomorphism $e_1:\mathcal{M}_1.C\cong C_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}k$, and assume the open subscheme of $\mathcal{M}_1.C$ obtained by pulling back along $e_1$ followed by $i_1$ followed by the first projection the open image of the $j$-finite chart $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is nonempty. The assertion is that every element of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\mathrm{Ig}/k)$, the degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones, lies in the subgroup generated by the classes of divisors $[\,\mathrm{plc}(c)\,]-[\,\mathrm{plc}(c')\,]$ of degree zero, where $c,c'$ range over $k$-points of $C_1$ (sections of $c_1$) whose images avoid the range of the projection from $C_1\times_XC_2$ and whose images in the $k$-fibre of the two-chart model lie in the range of $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$, and where $\mathrm{plc}$ denotes the place of $\mathrm{Ig}/k$ attached by $\mathcal{M}_1.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ to the corresponding $k$-point of $\mathcal{M}_1.C$ transported by $e_1^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the moving lemma for $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of a curve over an algebraically closed field, applied to the Igusa curve realised as the component $C_1$ of the mod-$p$ fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$: the degree-zero divisor classes are generated by differences of points chosen away from the finite set of bad points, namely the crossings with the other component and the complement of the $j$-finite chart. It supplies the generators on which the Frobenius and Hecke computations for the mod-$p$ fibre of $X_1(Mp)$ are carried out in the statements that cite it.
